#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527264} :activity/id #uuid "14fa4da3-db56-52d2-9f88-608a139f9065" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049728 :topic/id #uuid "0e84f145-35c9-580b-bb72-93e90f0414bb" :topic/math-academy-id 3052} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527260 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527178 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18626b8c-2493-5d55-9463-bd9f28fb30c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526554} {:answer/id #uuid "1adf42e3-1c70-5503-860d-6962e69cc281" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526560} {:answer/id #uuid "22d83ace-ef87-55ef-a2c4-9b139c05acd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526577} {:answer/id #uuid "d5612858-da5d-5749-b4be-3afeccbaa11a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526913} {:answer/id #uuid "d7f6b48f-b583-53c7-8275-d83bc842c8f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526919}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526560} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4504051-feaa-512b-9211-403c240f5138" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527102}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "86df2b6f-b298-58e2-a359-d3e3b918ef94" :question/math-academy-id "q-111250" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X>Y).$" :question/worked-solution "If $f(x,y)$ is a joint probability density function for the random variables $X$ and $Y$ and $A⊂{R}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\nP((X,Y)\\in A)={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonnegative in the region $D=[0,2]\\times [0,1],$ and the event $A=\\{X>Y\\}$ corresponds to a subset of $D,$ shown as the shaded region below:\n\n![](images/2d/2db85950b4d45901d79c173f264173d0c38046b2f087d0a28c8d5c69f024e31f.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>Y) & ={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∬}_{A}\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\text{Area}(A) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "778fed79-52b3-5022-a995-2a36a56152e4"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527264 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162298 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5bd480ea-cdb8-53d3-84bd-a013f43aa7a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245119} {:answer/id #uuid "780de2e0-4299-5e33-9543-d7971ad99051" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245379} {:answer/id #uuid "8c38e0fc-8dd7-5b64-9aac-7c29e0cf9a14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245544} {:answer/id #uuid "9829c0e8-c338-5c4b-b0d8-a76a88e02764" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245660} {:answer/id #uuid "c838d11c-aecd-5ce8-a87a-0a66b3789df4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246089}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245544} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d80915f-bae6-51ab-82d2-10b8ac22e0f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246770}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7e6281d3-4780-5346-a3c0-14376703344d" :question/math-academy-id "q-110366" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}cxy,\\, & 0\\le x\\le y<1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $c$ is a positive real number. Find the value of $c.$" :question/worked-solution "To verify that $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability density function, we must check the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$\n\n- ${∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y=1$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le y<1\\}.$\n\n![](images/01/01f3a8d99dd38ce2a728fe2cb4e4ab8de933ccd9ba27c87174779c428c303f48.png)\n\nNow, let's check our conditions:\n\n- Since $c>0,$ we clearly have $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ So the first condition is satisfied.\n\n- For the second condition to be satisfied, we must have \n\n$$\n{∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{x}^{1}cxy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nWe evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating  $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{x}^{1}cxy\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[cx\\cdot \\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=x}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{cx}{2}-\\frac{c{x}^{3}}{2})\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{cx}{2}-\\frac{c{x}^{3}}{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={[\\frac{c{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{c{x}^{4}}{8}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{c}{4}-\\frac{c}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{c}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{c}{8}=1\\,⇒\\,c=8.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "801fa807-3352-5bd1-814d-b25000e22228" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527273}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527273 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162300 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a22938f3-e3f3-5362-964f-f10b46383c24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245760} {:answer/id #uuid "a4b3cf30-4246-5293-a6ba-401dfbcd91dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245786} {:answer/id #uuid "ab559822-e626-5ec7-9216-e68dd31ae519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245846} {:answer/id #uuid "c4d201b6-473a-581f-a380-899fc82c3d13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246062} {:answer/id #uuid "ffb902c8-35bf-55d3-96c1-03b177b9d094" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246546}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246546} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc701cce-934a-56e4-afcf-8dabca6a89d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246940}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "79bec26d-9048-578e-8d3b-b8cd912ffc46" :question/math-academy-id "q-110368" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}c{x}^{2}y,\\, & {x}^{2}\\le y<1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhere $c$ is a positive real number. Find the value of $c.$" :question/worked-solution "To verify that $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability density function, we must check the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$\n\n- ${∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y=1$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}\\le y<1\\}.$\n\n![](images/b9/b9cfac7f0f82088900ab5e603588a73d4932f08f592321c797a1fd94b8bafb4e.png)\n\nNow, let's check our conditions:\n\n- Since $c>0,$ we clearly have $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ So the first condition is satisfied.\n\n- For the second condition to be satisfied, we must have \n\n$$\n{∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}c{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nWe evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating  $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}c{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{[c{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y={x}^{2}}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}c{x}^{2}(\\frac{1-{x}^{4}}{2})\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}c{x}^{2}(\\frac{1-{x}^{4}}{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={[c(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}-\\frac{{x}^{7}}{14})]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4c}{21}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{4c}{21}=1\\,⇒\\,c=\\frac{21}{4}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "a5964aa6-3d4d-5b0d-8edc-acec2fd46d0d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527277}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527277 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247211 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46e00eda-4098-5ea8-9286-1c659780d381" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.417" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244945} {:answer/id #uuid "794adeac-c0b1-576d-a547-3cbb8fd1ea50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.548" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245382} {:answer/id #uuid "79ca5e50-3240-55d0-b787-d6e3ab9623b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.613" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245387} {:answer/id #uuid "8acdfd26-6153-50a4-b247-82e1a51c91b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.827" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245530} {:answer/id #uuid "fc2f6765-7324-55dd-8d67-cc200672047c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.793" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246522}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246522} :answer-field/id #uuid "e46a81bb-da04-58df-8b73-5a6b912925ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246952}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "70065778-db0a-5680-ada4-1a1c95f48e99" :question/math-academy-id "q-111162" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y),\\, & 0\\le x\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}).$ Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "If $f(x,y)$ is a joint probability density function for the random variables $X$ and $Y$ and $A⊂{R}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\nP((X,Y)\\in A)={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonnegative in the region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}\\},$ and the event $A=\\{X\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}\\}$ corresponds to a subset of $D,$ shown as the shaded region below:\n\n![](images/ea/ea585fb6e12672f5cc854578cb12ff0357cfcd8d2f3d3b75a82723241cdaf3d4.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}) & ={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{\\int }_{x}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}y\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}[{\\int }_{x}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)]_{y=x}^{y=\\pi /2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2}))\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})]}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-0+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{3-\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & ≈0.793.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "c59b87d3-3574-5bfd-8921-7d04759f0077" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527282}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527282 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247214 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30e1a5e1-53dd-5405-b773-5096a99bef72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244752} {:answer/id #uuid "45642459-3fe9-5e9f-a372-085a1f846f33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244929} {:answer/id #uuid "5648d231-b525-59ab-a5e8-de881d67e6c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245074} {:answer/id #uuid "8228192e-4fc9-5017-8e03-1a47205cf78d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245463} {:answer/id #uuid "daf40184-bf74-5552-b396-a2c8bef81594" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246260}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244752} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea68a650-57c2-5481-9fd2-8ae6a75ff93a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246966}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "bdc40edd-ea5e-57db-9e7a-f82ff5703a98" :question/math-academy-id "q-111168" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X>1).$" :question/worked-solution "If $f(x,y)$ is a joint probability density function for the random variables $X$ and $Y$ and $A⊂{R}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\nP((X,Y)\\in A)={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonnegative in the region $D=[0,2]\\times [0,1],$ and the event $A=\\{X>1\\}$ corresponds to a subset of $D,$ shown as the shaded region below:\n\n![](images/26/26cbd44827c3a5a3fde5d61b631ce4f214bcf9a36ce6bf76129b1fe9f9478eff.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>1) & ={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∬}_{A}\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\text{Area}(A) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "e4e368b7-f8df-565c-b934-2de97cefe731" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527260}}] :activity/title "Joint Distributions for Continuous Random Variables" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526487}]}
